      "text": "For every finite raster B of pixels in Z^2, read with 8-connected barrier and a 4-connected complement taken in all of Z^2, the set of finite (enclosed) 4-components of Z^2 minus B is finite, and their number equals C8(B) - euler(B). C8 is the number of 8-components of B, and euler = V - E + F of the cubical complex of B (Candidate.main). The same file also proves L2 restated over these definitions (Candidate.insertion) and, as auxiliary theorems outside the sealed statement, that exactly one 4-component of the complement is infinite and that the total number of components is C8(B) - euler(B) + 1 (Candidate.unique_unbounded, Candidate.card_components).",
